desc: Breath Generator
// Designed by Rozaya, developed with Claude (Anthropic)
//
// This work is dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.
// https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LAYOUT 2026-09-08 (docs/layouts/breath-gen.md). 32 sliders -> 40, everything
// renumbered. Reading order: what it IS -> rate -> shape -> pitch -> fades ->
// stereo -> output -> transport -> drift -> ramp.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// --- Rate. NO rate mode, and that is deliberate ---------------------------
// The breath's rate is EMERGENT from its four segments, so there is no rate
// VALUE for a five-option mode to qualify. Same principled R20 exception Womb
// was granted 2026-09-06: forcing the five options on a breath produces
// "N per beat", and eight breaths per beat is not a thing anyone wants.
//
// A ONE-SHOT. Scales the four segments to the requested rate, preserving their
// ratio, then puts itself back to 0 so the four numbers on screen stay the
// truth. Never saves a value, so it can never fire on load.
slider1:0<0,1000,0.001>Set breath rate (per minute, or beats per breath; 0 = off)
// What the four segments below are counted in. Beats follows the project tempo.
slider2:0<0,1,1{Seconds,Beats}>Breath unit

// --- The shape of the breath, and its LENGTH: their sum IS the cycle -------
// Absolute durations, always, in the unit above -- which is why halving the
// inhale genuinely shortens the breath.
slider3:4.0<0.001,1000,0.001>Inhale (in breath units)
slider4:0.3<0,1000,0.001>Top pause (in breath units)
slider5:4.0<0.001,1000,0.001>Exhale (in breath units)
// Was 0..20 where its three siblings were 0..1000 -- the odd one out for no
// reason anyone recorded. Widened 2026-09-08; widening never moves a value.
slider6:0.3<0,1000,0.001>Bottom pause (in breath units)

// --- Pitch (R22). ONE block behind a target, never two --------------------
// These are FILTER CENTRES, and they get the block anyway -- Rozaya,
// 2026-09-08: "Filters: yes, they should. Musicality integration, not
// exclusivity, is the idea here."
//
// ONE pitch, expressed four ways -- Hz, semitones, cents, or a note name -- and
// exactly one fine tune. Rozaya, 2026-09-09: "note is not master here. it's one
// way of expressing pitch, period. Don't have two finetunes."
//
// FIRST BUILD OF R22 ANYWHERE IN THE SUITE. Breath Generator is the cheapest
// pitch case there is -- two filter centres, no per-voice banks, 4 instances --
// which is why it is the right place to find out whether the block feels right.
slider7:0<0,2,1{All,Inhale,Exhale}>Pitch target
// MODE FIRST, deliberately. It decides whether the note readout below means
// anything, so it has to be met first when tabbing through. This inverts R20's
// value-then-mode order on purpose -- Rozaya, 2026-09-09.
slider8:0<0,2,1{Hz,Semitones,Cents}>Pitch mode
// A REAL control, and it works BOTH ways. Semitones ARE note positions, so
// picking C4 and typing 60 say the same thing -- use whichever costs you less.
// Move either one and the other follows. Hidden outside Semitones mode, where it
// would be lying about a number that is a frequency or a cent count.
//
// The two-way binding is the shape that broke the rate block in August. It is
// safe here because the MIRROR says which end actually moved this pass, so
// nothing has to guess -- see the reconciliation in @slider.
slider9:60<0,127,1{C-1,C#-1,D-1,D#-1,E-1,F-1,F#-1,G-1,G#-1,A-1,A#-1,B-1,C0,C#0,D0,D#0,E0,F0,F#0,G0,G#0,A0,A#0,B0,C1,C#1,D1,D#1,E1,F1,F#1,G1,G#1,A1,A#1,B1,C2,C#2,D2,D#2,E2,F2,F#2,G2,G#2,A2,A#2,B2,C3,C#3,D3,D#3,E3,F3,F#3,G3,G#3,A3,A#3,B3,C4,C#4,D4,D#4,E4,F4,F#4,G4,G#4,A4,A#4,B4,C5,C#5,D5,D#5,E5,F5,F#5,G5,G#5,A5,A#5,B5,C6,C#6,D6,D#6,E6,F6,F#6,G6,G#6,A6,A#6,B6,C7,C#7,D7,D#7,E7,F7,F#7,G7,G#7,A7,A#7,B7,C8,C#8,D8,D#8,E8,F8,F#8,G8,G#8,A8,A#8,B8,C9,C#9,D9,D#9,E9,F9,F#9,G9}>Note name
// THE pitch, not an offset from anything. Hz is the frequency; Semitones is the
// MIDI note number, so 60 is middle C; Cents is the same axis x100.
//
// An earlier draft made this an OFFSET from a Note picker, which quietly turned
// it into a second fine tune sitting above the real one -- one job done twice,
// with the wrong half labelled as the coarse control. Rozaya, 2026-09-09:
// "note is not master here. it's one way of expressing pitch, period."
slider10:300<0,20000,0.001>Pitch value (Hz / semitones / cents)
// The only fine tune. There is exactly one, and it says what it is.
slider11:0<-1000,1000,0.001>Fine tune
slider12:2<0,2,1{Hz,Semitones,Cents}>Fine tune unit
slider13:440<20,2000,0.1>Tuning reference (Hz)

// --- Fades ----------------------------------------------------------------
slider14:0.3<0.0,1.0,0.01>Inhale fade in
slider15:0.2<0.0,1.0,0.01>Inhale fade out
slider16:0.2<0.0,1.0,0.01>Exhale fade in
slider17:0.3<0.0,1.0,0.01>Exhale fade out
slider18:2<1,4,1{Linear,Cosine,Exponential,Natural}>Fade mode

// --- Stereo ---------------------------------------------------------------
slider19:0.5<0.0,1.0,0.01>Stereo width
slider20:0<0,1,1{Normal,Flipped}>Stereo flip

// --- Output ---------------------------------------------------------------
// NEW 2026-09-08. Breath Generator had no output control of any kind, where
// every other plugin in the suite has one. Default 0 dB, so no existing
// instance changes level.
slider21:0<-60,12,0.01>Output (dB)

// --- Transport ------------------------------------------------------------
// Sit silent for N seconds after playback starts, then begin normally.
// Re-arms on every transport stop/start. 0 disables the delay.
slider22:0<0,1000,0.001>Start delay (seconds)
// Per-breath Play/Rest gate. Runs N full breath cycles, then sits silent for M
// breath cycles' worth of time, then repeats. During rest the state machine
// pauses on the bottom-pause state (already silent), so the gate's silence is
// just an extended bottom pause. The breath in progress finishes its natural
// envelope; the gate only stops the NEXT breath from starting. 0 in either
// disables it. Resets on every transport stop/start.
slider23:0<0,1000,1>Play for (breaths)
slider24:0<0,1000,1>Rest for (breaths)

// --- Drift (nested selector, per target) ----------------------------------
// Pick a target, then the controls below hold THAT target's config. All five
// targets drift in parallel; the selector only chooses which you are editing.
slider25:0<0,4,1{Inhale,Top pause,Exhale,Bottom pause,Breaths/min}>Drift target
// UNITS MATCH TARGET, corrected 2026-09-08. These said "(seconds)" and Breath
// Generator was the ONLY plugin in the suite that did -- the other eighteen say
// this. Its own target list includes Breaths/min, so "seconds" was lying for
// one of its five targets.
slider26:0<0,1000,0.01>Drift up amount (units match target)
slider27:0<0,1000,0.01>Drift down amount (units match target)
slider28:8<0,1000,1>Drift period (0 = off)
// What the period is COUNTED IN. Cycles is this plugin's native count -- one
// full breath, inhale through bottom pause -- and the default, which is exactly
// what this control did before the unit existed. Beats counts PROJECT tempo.
slider29:0<0,2,1{Cycles,Seconds,Beats}>Drift period unit
slider30:0<0,2,1{Sine,Triangle,Random}>Drift shape
// Counted in PERIODS. Both must be above zero or the gate is off. While resting
// the phase does not advance, so the offset FREEZES where it stopped rather
// than returning to centre -- and the FRACTION of the play value chooses where
// it parks: x.25 crest, x.75 trough, x.0 and x.5 neutral.
slider31:0<0,1000,0.01>Drift play for (periods, 0 = always)
slider32:0<0,1000,0.01>Drift rest for (periods, 0 = always)

// --- Ramp (nested selector, per target) -----------------------------------
// Ramp start delay rejoins its own block here. It sat at slider 32, seven
// places away, because it was appended later when append-only was the rule.
slider33:0<0,4,1{Inhale,Top pause,Exhale,Bottom pause,Breaths/min}>Ramp target
slider34:0<-1000,1000,0.001>Ramp by
// One unit for duration AND start delay, so they always mean the same as each
// other. DEFAULT IS 2, Minutes, which is what this block always did; index 0
// would silently reinterpret every saved ramp. Cycles counts whole breaths at
// the length BEFORE drift and ramp touch it, so a ramp cannot alter its own
// clock.
slider35:2<0,3,1{Cycles,Seconds,Minutes,Beats}>Ramp time unit
slider36:0<0,1000,0.1>Ramp duration (in ramp time units)
// The ramp advances for `play`, holds for `rest`, and repeats -- a staircase
// instead of a smooth glide. The holds come OUT of the duration rather than
// extending it, so Ramp duration goes on meaning "you arrive in about this
// long". Both zero is the smooth ramp.
slider37:0<0,1000,0.01>Ramp play for (0 = smooth)
slider38:0<0,1000,0.01>Ramp rest for (0 = smooth)
slider39:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Ramp engage
slider40:0<0,1000,0.1>Ramp start delay (in ramp time units)

@init
// v2.10 render-state fix (Path A — see docs/v2.9-render-state-bug.md).
// NO ext_noinit: REAPER re-runs @init on every transport play / render
// start, resetting all runtime state for free (state machine, filters,
// drift runtime, Speed Ramp, Start Delay, noise seeds). Only the drift +
// Speed Ramp CONFIG banks must survive the re-run; they're guarded by
// drift_cfg_inited below.

srate_inv = 1.0 / srate;
two_pi = 2.0 * $pi;

// State machine
// 0 = inhale, 1 = top pause, 2 = exhale, 3 = bottom pause
breath_state = 0;
state_phase = 0.0; // 0..1 through current state

// Durations in samples
inhale_len  = floor(srate * 4.0);
top_len     = floor(srate * 0.3);
exhale_len  = floor(srate * 4.0);
bot_len     = floor(srate * 0.3);
state_len   = inhale_len;
state_pos   = 0;

// Filter state - two channels, each with inhale and exhale filter
// L channel
in_lp_l = 0; in_bp_l = 0;
ex_lp_l = 0; ex_bp_l = 0;
// R channel - slightly different to decorrelate
in_lp_r = 0; in_bp_r = 0;
ex_lp_r = 0; ex_bp_r = 0;



// Filter coefficients - initialized to defaults
in_f  = min(2.0 * sin($pi * 800.0 * srate_inv), 0.98);
in_f_r = min(2.0 * sin($pi * 760.0 * srate_inv), 0.98);
ex_f  = min(2.0 * sin($pi * 600.0 * srate_inv), 0.98);
ex_f_r = min(2.0 * sin($pi * 560.0 * srate_inv), 0.98);
lp_q  = 0.6;

fade_in_in   = 0.3;
fade_in_out  = 0.2;
fade_ex_in   = 0.2;
fade_ex_out  = 0.3;
fade_mode    = 2;
stereo_width = 0.5;

noise_seed  = 12345;
noise_seed2 = 67890;

function apply_fade(pos, fade_in, fade_out, mode) local(raw, t) (
  // pos = 0..1 through the sound
  // fade_in and fade_out are fractions of total duration
  raw = 1.0;

  // Fade in region
  pos < fade_in ? (
    t = pos / fade_in; // 0..1 within fade
    mode == 1 ? raw = t;                                    // Linear
    mode == 2 ? raw = 0.5 - 0.5 * cos(t * $pi);           // Cosine
    mode == 3 ? raw = t * t;                               // Exponential in
    mode == 4 ? raw = sin(t * $pi * 0.5);                  // Natural (sine curve)
  ) :

  // Fade out region
  pos > (1.0 - fade_out) ? (
    t = (pos - (1.0 - fade_out)) / fade_out; // 0..1 within fade
    mode == 1 ? raw = 1.0 - t;
    mode == 2 ? raw = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(t * $pi);
    mode == 3 ? raw = (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t);
    mode == 4 ? raw = cos(t * $pi * 0.5);
  );

  raw;
);

// Start Delay state.
// (last_play_state removed in v2.10 Path A — no transport-edge handler
// anymore; @init re-running on play is the reset.)
start_delay_elapsed = 0;
start_delay_sec     = 0;

// Play/Rest gate state. pr_breath counts breaths completed in the
// current play period (init to 0 because the first breath is still
// in progress at t=0). pr_rest_elapsed counts samples spent in rest
// — when it reaches rest_for_breaths * total_breath_samples, exit
// rest and start a fresh breath cycle from inhale.
pr_resting          = 0;
pr_breath           = 0;
pr_rest_elapsed     = 0;
play_for_breaths    = 0;
rest_for_breaths    = 0;
pr_enabled          = 0;
total_breath_samples = 0;

// Speed ramp state. Per-target memory bank holds the signed `by` delta
// for each of 4 targets (Inhale, Top pause, Exhale, Bottom pause).
// @sample reads all 4 in parallel; the selector just edits which slot
// `Ramp by` currently reflects. ramp_t advances 0->1 over duration
// while engaged. Engage is a freeze/resume gate, NOT a restart edge —
// only transport play resets ramp_t.
// Engage (global) is a freeze/resume gate; only transport play resets the
// per-target ramp clocks. As of v2.14 the ramp is PER-TARGET: each target has
// its own `by`, duration, start delay, and progress clock (banks below).
N_SPEED_TARGETS              = 5;
speed_ramp_target_value_mem  = 4096;  // signed `by` per target (CONFIG)

// --- v2.9 Drift target memory banks ---
//
// 4 targets × 8 fields = 32 slots. Each array is 16-slot-aligned so
// there's room to grow targets later (up to 16) without re-laying-out.
// Speed ramp bank uses 4 slots starting at 4096; drift banks start
// at 4112 to keep the 16-slot alignment.
//
// Targets:
//   0 = Inhale Duration
//   1 = Top Pause
//   2 = Exhale Duration
//   3 = Bottom Pause
//   4 = Breaths/min (aggregate — scales all four segments in lockstep,
//       preserving I:E ratio; units = breaths per minute, signed)
N_TARGETS = 5;
target_drift_up     = 4112;
target_drift_down   = 4128;
target_drift_per    = 4144;
target_drift_shape  = 4160;
target_drift_phase  = 4176;
target_drift_prev   = 4192;
target_drift_curr   = 4208;
target_drift_offset = 4224;

// Speed ramp per-target timeline banks (v2.14). duration + start-delay are
// CONFIG (survive transport, restored by @serialize); ramp_t + delay_elapsed
// are RUNTIME (reset every @init / transport play).
speed_ramp_dur_mem           = 4240;  // duration minutes per target (CONFIG)
speed_ramp_delay_mem         = 4256;  // start-delay minutes per target (CONFIG)
speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem        = 4272;  // ramp progress 0..1 per target (RUNTIME)
speed_ramp_delay_elapsed_mem = 4288;  // delay sample counter per target (RUNTIME)

// Drift and Ramp play/rest, per target (2026-09-06). 16-slot-spaced like the
// banks above. play/rest are CONFIG (survive a transport re-init, restored by
// @serialize); accumulator and resting flag are RUNTIME. FIRST FREE SLOT AFTER
// THIS BLOCK IS 4432 -- re-derive rather than trusting this comment.
drift_play_mem       = 4304;
drift_rest_mem       = 4320;
sr_play_mem          = 4336;
sr_rest_mem          = 4352;
drift_pr_accum_mem   = 4368;
drift_pr_resting_mem = 4384;
sr_pr_accum_mem      = 4400;
sr_pr_resting_mem    = 4416;

// --- Pitch banks (R22, 2026-09-08) ----------------------------------------
// Targets: 0 = All (writes across), 1 = Inhale, 2 = Exhale. Only slots 1 and 2
// ever hold data; All is a writing convenience, exactly like Polyrhythm v3's
// Voice selector. FIRST FREE SLOT AFTER THIS BLOCK IS 4528 -- re-derive rather
// than trusting this comment.
N_PITCH        = 3;
pitch_note_mem = 4432;   // MIDI note 0..127            (CONFIG)
pitch_val_mem  = 4448;   // coarse offset               (CONFIG)
pitch_mode_mem = 4464;   // 0 Hz, 1 semitones, 2 cents  (CONFIG)
pitch_fine_mem = 4480;   // fine offset                 (CONFIG)
pitch_fmod_mem = 4496;   // fine mode                   (CONFIG)
pitch_hz_mem   = 4512;   // DERIVED in @block, never here
pui_last       = 4528;   // mirror of the five visible controls (RUNTIME)
pitch_ui_inited = 0;     // adopted in @block; while 0, @slider writes nothing

// --- The Pitch target selector's three operations -------------------------
// Lifted from Polyrhythm v3's Voice selector, which is the worked example for
// an `All` position. Reading is approximate, writing is exact.
function pitch_read_slot(psel) (
  psel > 0 ? psel : 1;          // All reads back from Inhale
);
function pitch_write(psel, pbank, pval) (
  psel > 0 ? (
    pbank[psel] = pval;
  ) : (
    pbank[1] = pval;
    pbank[2] = pval;
  );
);
// WRITE ONLY IF THE CONTROL ACTUALLY MOVED. This is what makes parking on All
// safe: a stray @slider pass during a project load writes nothing to either
// target. Without it, an instance saved on All would stamp the inhale
// frequency over the exhale one every single load -- silently, and the blob
// would then be re-saved with the damage.
function pitch_capture(psel, pbank, pval, pslot) (
  pval != pui_last[pslot] ? (
    pitch_write(psel, pbank, pval);
    pui_last[pslot] = pval;
  );
);

// Seeds so nothing reads a zero if a block ever runs oddly. @block overwrites
// breath_unit_sec and the derived pitches every block.
// SEEDED, and it matters: pitch_to_hz() reads tuning_ref and is called from
// @block, which can run before @slider has ever run. Unseeded it is 0, which
// puts every note at 0 Hz and parks both filters on the 20 Hz clamp.
tuning_ref       = 440;
breath_unit      = 0;
breath_unit_sec  = 1;
breath_set_ready = 0;    // the one-shot cannot fire until @block arms it
out_gain         = 1;

// Resolve one pitch target to Hz. Note first, then the coarse pair as an OFFSET
// from that note, then the fine pair on top. Hz is an offset rather than an
// absolute, which is what lets the migration keep an old frequency exactly
// while still naming a note for it.
function pitch_to_hz(idx) local(m, v, f, fm, hz) (
  // The value IS the pitch. Hz is the frequency; Semitones is the MIDI note
  // number (60 = middle C); Cents is the same axis at x100. Nothing here is an
  // offset from anything -- that was the shape that turned this into a second
  // fine tune.
  m = pitch_mode_mem[idx];
  v = pitch_val_mem[idx];
  hz = m == 1 ? tuning_ref * pow(2, (v - 69) / 12) :
       m == 2 ? tuning_ref * pow(2, (v / 100 - 69) / 12) :
                v;
  // The ONE fine tune, in its own unit, applied on top.
  fm = pitch_fmod_mem[idx];
  f  = pitch_fine_mem[idx];
  hz = fm == 1 ? hz * pow(2, f / 12) :
       fm == 2 ? hz * pow(2, f / 1200) :
                 hz + f;
  // Clamped to what the FILTER can honour, not to the audible band.
  min(max(hz, 1), 20000);
);

// Shared play/rest gate, byte-identical to the one in Melody, the Sweeping
// Filter, Tremolo, Phaser, Bubbler, Dapple, Resonance Bank and the Morpher.
// `tick` is how much of one play/rest unit passes per sample, so the caller owns
// the unit and this stays unitless. Returns 1 while the target is resting.
function pr_frozen(accum_bank, resting_bank, idx, tick, play, rest) (
  play > 0 && rest > 0 ? (
    accum_bank[idx] += tick;
    accum_bank[idx] >= (resting_bank[idx] ? rest : play) ? (
      accum_bank[idx] = 0;
      resting_bank[idx] = 1 - resting_bank[idx];
    );
    resting_bank[idx];
  ) : ( 0; );
);

// CONFIG banks (drift up/down/period/shape + the Speed Ramp by/duration/
// start-delay banks + selector trackers) — initialized ONCE per instance,
// guarded by drift_cfg_inited so the @init re-run on every transport play
// (Path A render fix, no ext_noinit) does NOT wipe the user's setup.
// @serialize below restores saved configs on project reload.
drift_cfg_inited != 1 ? (
  i = 0;
  loop(N_SPEED_TARGETS,
    speed_ramp_target_value_mem[i] = 0;
    drift_play_mem[i] = 0; drift_rest_mem[i] = 0;
    sr_play_mem[i]    = 0; sr_rest_mem[i]    = 0;
    speed_ramp_dur_mem[i]          = 0;
    speed_ramp_delay_mem[i]        = 0;
    i += 1;
  );
  last_speed_target = 0;
  i = 0;
  loop(N_TARGETS,
    target_drift_up[i]    = 0;
    target_drift_down[i]  = 0;
    target_drift_per[i]   = 8;
    target_drift_shape[i] = 0;
    i += 1;
  );
  last_target_select = 0;

  // Pitch defaults reproduce the two frequencies this plugin has always had:
  // 800 Hz inhale and 600 Hz exhale, expressed as the nearest note at or below
  // plus an exact Hz remainder. A fresh instance sounds identical to before.
  // The two filter centres this plugin has always had, said plainly now that
  // the value is the pitch: 800 Hz in, 600 Hz out.
  pitch_val_mem[1] = 800; pitch_note_mem[1] = 79;
  pitch_val_mem[2] = 600; pitch_note_mem[2] = 74;
  i = 0;
  loop(N_PITCH,
    pitch_mode_mem[i] = 0;
    pitch_fine_mem[i] = 0;
    pitch_fmod_mem[i] = 0;
    i += 1;
  );
  pitch_val_mem[0] = 800; pitch_note_mem[0] = 79;
  last_pitch_target = 0;

  drift_cfg_inited = 1;
);

// Drift + speed-ramp RUNTIME resets on EVERY @init — i.e. every transport
// play — restoring the v2.8 fresh-play behavior. Drift phase seeded per-target
// with rand(1) so the four drifts don't all crest together.
i = 0;
loop(N_SPEED_TARGETS,
  speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[i]        = 0;
  speed_ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[i] = 0;
  drift_pr_accum_mem[i] = 0; drift_pr_resting_mem[i] = 0;
  sr_pr_accum_mem[i]    = 0; sr_pr_resting_mem[i]    = 0;
  i += 1;
);
i = 0;
loop(N_TARGETS,
  target_drift_phase[i]  = rand(1);
  target_drift_prev[i]   = 0;
  target_drift_curr[i]   = 0;
  target_drift_offset[i] = 0;
  i += 1;
);

@slider
inhale_len = max(floor(srate * slider3), 1);
top_len    = max(floor(srate * slider4), 1);
exhale_len = max(floor(srate * slider5), 1);
bot_len    = max(floor(srate * slider6), 1);

// Clamp state_pos if durations shrank
breath_state == 0 ? state_len = inhale_len;
breath_state == 1 ? state_len = top_len;
breath_state == 2 ? state_len = exhale_len;
breath_state == 3 ? state_len = bot_len;
state_pos = min(state_pos, state_len - 1);

// Width spreads L and R filter frequencies apart from center
// The four filter coefficients MOVED TO @block on 2026-09-08. They now derive
// from the pitch BANKS, which @serialize restores by an independent path with
// no guaranteed order against @slider -- so computing them here would leave
// them stale on load while every saved value sat correct in the bank. The
// symptom of getting this wrong is unmistakable and has bitten three plugins
// here: touching any control fixes it, transport play does not.

tuning_ref = slider13;
breath_unit = slider2;
out_gain = pow(10, slider21 / 20);

// --- Set breath rate: the ONE-SHOT ----------------------------------------
// Scales the four segments to the requested rate, preserving their ratio, then
// puts itself back to 0 so the four numbers on screen stay the truth.
//
// GUARDED ON breath_set_ready, WHICH IS ADOPTED IN @block AND NOT HERE. On a
// fresh or duplicated instance @slider runs while REAPER is still handing over
// saved values, so a flag adopted here takes a default and the real value
// arriving a moment later reads as a user edit -- which is how a picker came to
// stamp a hand-set rate on every load (proved 2026-08-23). While the flag is 0
// this fires nothing at all, which is the safe direction.
//
// It also cannot fire on a saved value, because it never saves one: it zeroes
// itself after every use and the migration seeds it to 0.
breath_set_ready && slider1 > 0 ? (
  bs_total = slider3 + slider4 + slider5 + slider6;
  bs_total > 0.001 ? (
    // The target cycle IN THE SEGMENTS' OWN UNIT. Seconds: the control is
    // breaths per minute, so one breath is 60/rate seconds. Beats: the control
    // is already beats per breath, so it IS the target.
    bs_target = breath_unit == 0 ? 60 / max(slider1, 0.001) : slider1;
    bs_k = bs_target / bs_total;
    slider3 = min(1000, max(0.001, slider3 * bs_k));
    slider4 = min(1000, max(0,     slider4 * bs_k));
    slider5 = min(1000, max(0.001, slider5 * bs_k));
    slider6 = min(1000, max(0,     slider6 * bs_k));
  );
  slider1 = 0;
  // sliderchange, NOT slider_automate: makes the values stick and refreshes the
  // display without writing automation the user never asked for.
  sliderchange(-1);
);

// --- Pitch target selector -------------------------------------------------
// Change-detected, and gated on a flag adopted in @block. While the flag is 0
// this writes nothing at all, which is the safe direction on a fresh or
// duplicated instance -- @slider runs there while REAPER is still handing over
// saved values, and an unguarded write would capture defaults as if the user
// had typed them (proved 2026-08-23).
pitch_ui_inited ? (
  sel_pitch = slider7;
  last_pitch_target != sel_pitch ? (
    prs = pitch_read_slot(sel_pitch);
    slider8  = pitch_mode_mem[prs];
    slider9  = pitch_note_mem[prs];
    slider10 = pitch_val_mem[prs];
    slider11 = pitch_fine_mem[prs];
    slider12 = pitch_fmod_mem[prs];
    slider_automate(slider8);
    slider_automate(slider9);
    slider_automate(slider10);
    slider_automate(slider11);
    slider_automate(slider12);
    // Refresh the mirror to what was just loaded, so the next pass does not
    // read the load as five user edits.
    pui_last[0] = slider8;  pui_last[1] = slider9;
    pui_last[2] = slider10; pui_last[3] = slider11;
    pui_last[4] = slider12;
    last_pitch_target = sel_pitch;
  ) : (
    // RECONCILE THE PAIR FIRST, then capture. The other order banks the stale
    // half: pick a note, and the bank would take the old value for one pass and
    // the sound would lag the display by an edit.
    //
    // The note name is a REAL control, not a readout -- semitones ARE note
    // positions, so picking C4 and typing 60 are two ways of saying the same
    // thing, and you use whichever costs you less.
    //
    // This is a two-way binding, the shape that broke the rate block in August,
    // so it is done the one way that is safe: the MIRROR says which end the user
    // actually moved. Nothing guesses. REAPER fires @slider per parameter
    // change, so only one end moves at a time, and the mirror is adopted in
    // @block where it cannot capture a default.
    slider8 == 1 ? (
      slider9 != pui_last[1] ? (
        slider10 = slider9;             // a note was picked; it IS the pitch
        sliderchange(-1);
      ) : (
        pn = min(127, max(0, floor(slider10 + 0.5)));
        pn != slider9 ? ( slider9 = pn; sliderchange(-1); );
      );
    );
    pitch_capture(sel_pitch, pitch_mode_mem, slider8,  0);
    pitch_capture(sel_pitch, pitch_note_mem, slider9,  1);
    pitch_capture(sel_pitch, pitch_val_mem,  slider10, 2);
    pitch_capture(sel_pitch, pitch_fine_mem, slider11, 3);
    pitch_capture(sel_pitch, pitch_fmod_mem, slider12, 4);
  );
);

// Hide the note name outside Semitones mode, where it would be lying about a
// number that is a frequency or a cent count.
slider_show(slider9, slider8 == 1);

fade_in_in  = slider14;
fade_in_out = slider15;
fade_ex_in  = slider16;
fade_ex_out = slider17;
fade_mode   = slider18;
stereo_width = slider19;

start_delay_sec = slider22;

// Play/Rest gate: integer breath counts. Both must be > 0 for the
// gate to engage. total_breath_samples is the sample-count of one
// full breath cycle, used to time the rest period (which is a
// continuous sample counter, not a state-machine count).
total_breath_samples = inhale_len + top_len + exhale_len + bot_len;
play_for_breaths = slider23;
rest_for_breaths = slider24;
new_pr_enabled = (play_for_breaths > 0 && rest_for_breaths > 0);
// If the user disables the gate mid-rest, snap back to the start of
// a fresh inhale so the plugin doesn't stay stuck silent in state 3.
!new_pr_enabled && pr_resting ? (
  pr_resting = 0;
  breath_state = 0;
  state_len = inhale_len;
  state_pos = 0;
);
pr_enabled = new_pr_enabled;

// Speed ramp target selector save/restore. slider33 = target; slider34 =
// per-target `by`; slider36 = per-target duration; slider40 = per-target start
// delay (all three per-target as of v2.14). slider39 (engage) stays GLOBAL.
// When the selector changes, save the three per-target sliders to the OLD
// slot, then load the NEW slot's stored values. Otherwise capture live edits.
sel_speed_target = slider33;
last_speed_target != sel_speed_target ? (
  speed_ramp_target_value_mem[last_speed_target] = slider34;
  speed_ramp_dur_mem[last_speed_target]          = slider36;
  speed_ramp_delay_mem[last_speed_target]        = slider40;
  sr_play_mem[last_speed_target]                 = slider37;
  sr_rest_mem[last_speed_target]                 = slider38;
  slider34 = speed_ramp_target_value_mem[sel_speed_target];
  slider36 = speed_ramp_dur_mem[sel_speed_target];
  slider40 = speed_ramp_delay_mem[sel_speed_target];
  slider_automate(slider34);
  slider_automate(slider36);
  slider37 = sr_play_mem[sel_speed_target];
  slider38 = sr_rest_mem[sel_speed_target];
  slider_automate(slider40);
  slider_automate(slider37);
  slider_automate(slider38);
  last_speed_target = sel_speed_target;
) : (
  speed_ramp_target_value_mem[sel_speed_target] = slider34;
  speed_ramp_dur_mem[sel_speed_target]          = slider36;
  speed_ramp_delay_mem[sel_speed_target]        = slider40;
  sr_play_mem[sel_speed_target]                 = slider37;
  sr_rest_mem[sel_speed_target]                 = slider38;
);
// No engage-edge detection. `Ramp engage` (global) is a freeze/resume
// gate, handled in @sample by advancing each target's own ramp clock.

// Drift target selector save/restore. Same nested-selector pattern as
// Speed Ramp above: when the user switches targets, save sliders 22-25
// into the OLD target's slot, then load the NEW target's stored config
// into sliders 22-25. When the selector hasn't changed, capture live
// edits into the current slot. All 4 targets drift in parallel from
// @sample regardless of which is selected here.
sel_target = slider25;
sel_up     = slider26;
sel_down   = slider27;
sel_per    = slider28;
sel_shape  = slider30;
sel_dplay  = slider31;
sel_drest  = slider32;

last_target_select != sel_target ? (
  target_drift_up[last_target_select]    = sel_up;
  target_drift_down[last_target_select]  = sel_down;
  target_drift_per[last_target_select]   = sel_per;
  target_drift_shape[last_target_select] = sel_shape;
  drift_play_mem[last_target_select]     = sel_dplay;
  drift_rest_mem[last_target_select]     = sel_drest;

  slider26 = target_drift_up[sel_target];
  slider27 = target_drift_down[sel_target];
  slider28 = target_drift_per[sel_target];
  slider30 = target_drift_shape[sel_target];
  slider_automate(slider26);
  slider_automate(slider27);
  slider_automate(slider28);
  slider31 = drift_play_mem[sel_target];
  slider32 = drift_rest_mem[sel_target];
  slider_automate(slider30);
  slider_automate(slider31);
  slider_automate(slider32);

  last_target_select = sel_target;
) : (
  target_drift_up[sel_target]    = sel_up;
  target_drift_down[sel_target]  = sel_down;
  target_drift_per[sel_target]   = sel_per;
  target_drift_shape[sel_target] = sel_shape;
  drift_play_mem[sel_target]     = sel_dplay;
  drift_rest_mem[sel_target]     = sel_drest;
);

@block
// --- Adopted here, never in @slider ---------------------------------------
// @block cannot run before the instance is configured, so this arms the
// one-shot only once REAPER has finished handing over saved values. Adopting
// it in @slider would let a default fire it.
breath_set_ready = 1;

// Adopt the pitch UI mirror from the RAW sliders, once, here rather than in
// @slider. @block cannot run before the instance is configured, so this reads
// settled values whatever order the restore paths ran in.
!pitch_ui_inited ? (
  pui_last[0] = slider8;  pui_last[1] = slider9;
  pui_last[2] = slider10; pui_last[3] = slider11;
  pui_last[4] = slider12;
  last_pitch_target = slider7;
  pitch_ui_inited = 1;
);

// What one breath unit is worth in SECONDS. Recomputed every block so a live
// tempo change is followed rather than remembered -- the `@init` re-runs on
// transport play, so anything that remembers a tempo loses it.
breath_unit_sec = breath_unit == 1 ? 60 / max(tempo, 0.001) : 1;

// --- Pitch, DERIVED FROM THE BANKS, so it belongs here --------------------
// Not in @slider. A value derived from a bank that @serialize restores must be
// computed in @block, because the two restore paths have no guaranteed order:
// @slider running first would derive from @init defaults and nothing would
// recompute when the bank filled in underneath.
pitch_hz_mem[1] = pitch_to_hz(1);
pitch_hz_mem[2] = pitch_to_hz(2);

// Stereo width spreads L and R filter centres apart. Unchanged in behaviour --
// only the source of the two centre frequencies moved.
in_f   = min(2.0 * sin($pi * (pitch_hz_mem[1] * (1.0 + stereo_width * 0.15)) * srate_inv), 0.98);
in_f_r = min(2.0 * sin($pi * (pitch_hz_mem[1] * (1.0 - stereo_width * 0.15)) * srate_inv), 0.98);
ex_f   = min(2.0 * sin($pi * (pitch_hz_mem[2] * (1.0 + stereo_width * 0.12)) * srate_inv), 0.98);
ex_f_r = min(2.0 * sin($pi * (pitch_hz_mem[2] * (1.0 - stereo_width * 0.12)) * srate_inv), 0.98);

@sample

// (No transport-edge reset here — Path A. REAPER re-runs @init on every
// transport play / render start, which resets all runtime state — state
// machine, filters, drift runtime, Speed Ramp, Start Delay, Play/Rest
// counters, noise seeds; the CONFIG banks are preserved across those
// re-runs by the drift_cfg_inited guard in @init. See
// docs/v2.9-render-state-bug.md.)

// Advance each target's own ramp clock (v2.14 per-target timeline). Engage
// (slider39, GLOBAL) is the freeze/resume gate: while On, each target whose
// duration > 0 advances its own ramp_t 0->1 over its own duration, after its
// own start delay; while Off, all clocks freeze and resume. Only transport
// play (via @init) resets them.
slider39 ? (
  i = 0;
  // Ramp time unit (slider35). One factor turns the block's time values into
  // seconds, so Duration and Start delay always mean the same as each other.
  // Cycles is one whole breath. Beats is 60/project tempo, recomputed per sample
  // so it follows a live tempo change rather than remembering one.
  ramp_time_scale =
    slider35 == 3 ? 60 / max(tempo, 0.001) :
    slider35 == 2 ? 60 :
    slider35 == 1 ? 1 :
                    max(total_breath_samples, 1) / srate;
  loop(N_SPEED_TARGETS,
    speed_ramp_dur_mem[i] > 0 ? (
      sr_delay_samples = speed_ramp_delay_mem[i] * ramp_time_scale * srate;
      speed_ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[i] < sr_delay_samples ? (
        speed_ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[i] += 1;
      ) : (
        // Staircase: advance for `play`, hold for `rest`, repeat. The holds come
        // OUT of the duration rather than extending it -- the advancing step is
        // scaled by (play+rest)/play -- so Ramp duration goes on meaning "you
        // arrive in about this long".
        sr_pl = sr_play_mem[i];
        sr_rs = sr_rest_mem[i];
        sr_pr_on = sr_pl > 0 && sr_rs > 0;
        sr_hold = pr_frozen(sr_pr_accum_mem, sr_pr_resting_mem, i,
                            1.0 / (ramp_time_scale * srate), sr_pl, sr_rs);
        // One-armed on purpose -- an empty else-branch is a silent compile
        // failure in eel2 (CLAUDE.md).
        !sr_hold ? (
          sr_step = 1.0 / (srate * speed_ramp_dur_mem[i] * ramp_time_scale);
          sr_pr_on ? sr_step *= (sr_pl + sr_rs) / sr_pl;
          speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[i] += sr_step;
          speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[i] > 1.0 ? speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[i] = 1.0;
        );
      );
    );
    i += 1;
  );
);

// Per-target Speed Ramp offsets (parallel — all 5 ramp regardless of which
// target the selector is currently showing). Each target gets its own
// `ramp_t * stored_amount` in its native unit (seconds for breath segments;
// breaths/min for the aggregate target 4).
speed_ramp_inhale_offset = speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[0] * speed_ramp_target_value_mem[0];
speed_ramp_top_offset    = speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[1] * speed_ramp_target_value_mem[1];
speed_ramp_exhale_offset = speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[2] * speed_ramp_target_value_mem[2];
speed_ramp_bot_offset    = speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[3] * speed_ramp_target_value_mem[3];
speed_ramp_bpm_offset    = speed_ramp_ramp_t_mem[4] * speed_ramp_target_value_mem[4];

// Per-target drift wave computation. Each of 4 targets gets a phase
// counter advancing per sample at rate 1 / (period_cycles * one_cycle_samples).
// Period unit is breath cycles for all 4 targets. Drift offset for each
// target is computed in seconds and stored back into target_drift_offset[i]
// for use in the segment-length computation below. The drift block uses
// total_breath_samples from the PREVIOUS sample's computation (a 1-sample
// lag, acoustically negligible) — total_breath_samples is recomputed
// after segment lengths are applied below.
i = 0;
loop(N_TARGETS,
  up    = target_drift_up[i];
  down  = target_drift_down[i];
  per   = target_drift_per[i];
  shape = target_drift_shape[i];

  drift_offset_local = 0;
  (up > 0 || down > 0) && per > 0 ? (
    // Drift period unit (slider29). Cycles is one whole breath, which is what
    // this control always counted. Seconds is wall clock. Beats counts the
    // PROJECT tempo.
    period_samples =
      slider29 == 2 ? max(per * 60 / max(tempo, 0.001) * srate, 1) :
      slider29 == 1 ? max(per * srate, 1) :
                      max(per * max(total_breath_samples, 1), 1);

    // Drift play/rest, per target, counted in PERIODS. While resting the phase
    // does not advance at all, so the offset FREEZES where it stopped rather
    // than returning to centre.
    d_frozen = pr_frozen(drift_pr_accum_mem, drift_pr_resting_mem, i,
                         1.0 / period_samples,
                         drift_play_mem[i], drift_rest_mem[i]);
    // One-armed pairs: an empty else-branch is a silent compile failure in eel2.
    d_frozen ? ( new_phase = target_drift_phase[i]; );
    !d_frozen ? (
      new_phase = target_drift_phase[i] + 1.0 / period_samples;
      new_phase >= 1.0 ? (
        new_phase -= 1.0;
        shape == 2 ? (
          target_drift_prev[i] = target_drift_curr[i];
          target_drift_curr[i] = rand(2) - 1;
        );
      );
    );
    target_drift_phase[i] = new_phase;

    shape == 0 ? (
      shape_val = sin(2 * $pi * new_phase);
    ) : shape == 1 ? (
      shape_val = new_phase < 0.25 ? (4 * new_phase) :
                  new_phase < 0.75 ? (2 - 4 * new_phase) :
                                     (4 * new_phase - 4);
    ) : (
      shape_val = target_drift_prev[i] +
        (target_drift_curr[i] - target_drift_prev[i]) * new_phase;
    );
    drift_offset_local = shape_val > 0 ? shape_val * up : shape_val * down;
  );
  target_drift_offset[i] = drift_offset_local;
  i += 1;
);

// Breaths/min aggregate (target 4): a proportional scale across ALL four
// segments in lockstep, preserving the I:E ratio (the Job B ratio-aggregate).
// Combined breath-rate delta (drift + Speed Ramp, in breaths/min) shifts the
// whole breath rate; each segment is divided by the scale (faster rate =
// shorter segments). Composes with the per-segment drift + ramp offsets.
// breath_unit_sec turns the segments' own unit into seconds (1 in Seconds,
// 60/tempo in Beats), so everything below is unchanged arithmetic on seconds.
base_breath_total = max((slider3 + slider4 + slider5 + slider6) * breath_unit_sec, 0.001);
base_breath_rate  = 60 / base_breath_total;
breath_rate_delta = target_drift_offset[4] + speed_ramp_bpm_offset;
breath_rate_scale = max(base_breath_rate + breath_rate_delta, 0.001) / base_breath_rate;

// Effective per-segment lengths: baseline (from slider) + Speed Ramp
// offset + per-target drift offset, then the Breaths/min aggregate scale.
// These OVERWRITE the @slider-set values each sample so that Speed Ramp's
// continuous progress, drift wander, and rate aggregate are all reflected
// in segment length at every sample.
inhale_len = max(floor(srate * breath_unit_sec * max((slider3 + speed_ramp_inhale_offset + target_drift_offset[0]) / breath_rate_scale, 0.1)), 1);
top_len    = max(floor(srate * breath_unit_sec * max((slider4 + speed_ramp_top_offset    + target_drift_offset[1]) / breath_rate_scale, 0  )), 1);
exhale_len = max(floor(srate * breath_unit_sec * max((slider5 + speed_ramp_exhale_offset + target_drift_offset[2]) / breath_rate_scale, 0.1)), 1);
bot_len    = max(floor(srate * breath_unit_sec * max((slider6 + speed_ramp_bot_offset    + target_drift_offset[3]) / breath_rate_scale, 0  )), 1);
total_breath_samples = inhale_len + top_len + exhale_len + bot_len;

// (Path A: @init re-runs on transport play and resets all runtime —
// start_delay_elapsed, the per-target ramp clocks, drift phases. No
// explicit transport-edge handler here.)

start_delay_elapsed < start_delay_sec ? (
  start_delay_elapsed += 1 / srate;
  spl0 = 0;
  spl1 = 0;
) : (

// Advance state machine. The 3→0 transition (end of bottom pause,
// start of a new breath cycle) is special-cased so the Play/Rest
// gate can decide whether to actually start a new breath or stay
// silent in state 3 for the rest of the rest period.
//
// State machine advances at 1× sample-rate; segment lengths carry any
// drift or Speed Ramp offset (applied above). Drift was previously
// rolled into a combined_scale multiplier on state_pos; v2.9 moved
// drift to additive offsets on the segment lengths themselves, so
// state_pos just advances by 1 here.
state_pos += 1;
state_pos >= state_len ? (
  state_pos = 0;
  breath_state == 3 ? (
    // End of bottom pause — would normally start a new breath.
    // First: did the breath we JUST completed take us to the play
    // threshold? If so, flip to rest. (Only counts when actually
    // playing — during rest, repeated state-3 ends don't increment
    // the breath counter.)
    pr_enabled && !pr_resting ? (
      pr_breath += 1;
      pr_breath >= play_for_breaths ? (
        pr_resting = 1;
        pr_breath = 0;
        pr_rest_elapsed = 0;
      );
    );
    // Start a new breath cycle ONLY if not resting. If pr_resting is
    // true (either we just flipped to rest, or we've been resting),
    // leave breath_state at 3 and state_pos at 0 so the next pass
    // through the state-end check just re-enters the bottom pause
    // (already silent). The rest timer below is what eventually
    // exits rest and forces a fresh inhale.
    !pr_resting ? (
      breath_state = 0;
      state_len = inhale_len;
    );
  ) : (
    // Normal advance within a breath (0→1, 1→2, 2→3).
    breath_state = (breath_state + 1) % 4;
    breath_state == 1 ? state_len = top_len;
    breath_state == 2 ? state_len = exhale_len;
    breath_state == 3 ? state_len = bot_len;
  );
);

// Rest timer. While resting, count samples elapsed since rest
// began. When that reaches rest_for_breaths * total_breath_samples,
// exit rest and force a fresh inhale to start. total_breath_samples
// is recomputed in @slider whenever any phase-duration slider
// changes, so changing those mid-rest stretches/compresses the
// remaining rest accordingly.
pr_resting ? (
  // Rest timer advances at 1× sample-rate; rest duration
  // (rest_for_breaths * total_breath_samples) already accounts for
  // any drift / Speed Ramp wander on the breath cycle (since
  // total_breath_samples is recomputed from drifted segment lengths
  // above each sample). So the play/rest ratio stays consistent.
  pr_rest_elapsed += 1;
  pr_rest_elapsed >= rest_for_breaths * total_breath_samples ? (
    pr_resting = 0;
    pr_breath = 0;
    breath_state = 0;
    state_len = inhale_len;
    state_pos = 0;
  );
);

// Position within current state as 0..1
state_phase = state_pos / max(state_len - 1, 1);

// Independent white noise per channel via Park-Miller / MINSTD generators
// (Lehmer LCG): x = (x * a) mod (2^31 - 1). EEL2 does ALL math in float64,
// where integers are exact only below 2^53 — so an LCG multiply must keep
// a * x under that ceiling or it silently rounds. Park-Miller's
// a * modulus is ~1.0e14 (48271) / 1.5e14 (69621), a ~60-90x margin under
// 2^53 = 9.0e15, so the multiply is always exact. The original right
// channel used a power-of-2 LCG with multiplier 22695477, whose product
// 22695477 * 2^32 = 9.7e16 OVERFLOWED 2^53 — the rounded multiply
// degenerated the sequence into an audible periodic tone + DC offset on
// the right channel only. The prime modulus also gives a full period with
// no low-bit patterning. The two channels use DIFFERENT multipliers
// (48271 / 69621, both standard MINSTD constants) so they are genuinely
// independent, not phase-shifted copies of one stream. Seeds must be
// nonzero in [1, 2^31-2] (set in @init; reset there every play).
noise_seed  = (noise_seed  * 48271) % 2147483647;
nl = noise_seed  * (2.0 / 2147483647.0) - 1.0;
noise_seed2 = (noise_seed2 * 69621) % 2147483647;
nr = noise_seed2 * (2.0 / 2147483647.0) - 1.0;

// Silence during pauses
(breath_state == 1 || breath_state == 3) ? (
  spl0 = 0;
  spl1 = 0;
) : (

  breath_state == 0 ? (
    // Inhale
    env = apply_fade(state_phase, fade_in_in, fade_in_out, fade_mode);

    // L
    in_lp_l += in_f * in_bp_l;
    in_hp_l = nl - in_lp_l - lp_q * in_bp_l;
    in_bp_l += in_f * in_hp_l;

    // R - different f coefficient for width
    in_lp_r += in_f_r * in_bp_r;
    in_hp_r = nr - in_lp_r - lp_q * in_bp_r;
    in_bp_r += in_f_r * in_hp_r;

    slider20 == 0 ? (
      spl0 = in_lp_l * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
      spl1 = in_lp_r * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
    ) : (
      spl0 = in_lp_r * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
      spl1 = in_lp_l * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
    );
  ) : (
    // Exhale
    env = apply_fade(state_phase, fade_ex_in, fade_ex_out, fade_mode);

    ex_lp_l += ex_f * ex_bp_l;
    ex_hp_l = nl - ex_lp_l - lp_q * ex_bp_l;
    ex_bp_l += ex_f * ex_hp_l;

    ex_lp_r += ex_f_r * ex_bp_r;
    ex_hp_r = nr - ex_lp_r - lp_q * ex_bp_r;
    ex_bp_r += ex_f_r * ex_hp_r;

    slider20 == 0 ? (
      spl0 = ex_lp_l * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
      spl1 = ex_lp_r * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
    ) : (
      spl0 = ex_lp_r * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
      spl1 = ex_lp_l * env * 1.5 * out_gain;
    );
  );
);

);  // close start-delay else branch

@serialize
// Persist per-target Speed Ramp (by / duration / start-delay) + drift configs
// so reload restores all targets, not just whichever was selected at save.
//
// VERSION-GUARDED (CLAUDE.md @serialize gotcha; NEW in v2.14 — breath's stream
// was previously unversioned). Magic = 2100000 + N_TARGETS marks the
// per-target-timeline format (added the duration + start-delay banks). Older
// (unversioned) blobs won't match and fall through to @init defaults — drift +
// ramp reset on upgrade (accepted; pre-release). Marker is float32-exact.
// 2026-09-06: four per-target banks added (Drift play/rest, Ramp play/rest), so
// the magic bumps and the READ accepts BOTH. A bump rather than a bare append,
// because appending would let an older blob's trailing bytes land in the new
// banks -- "migrate what was RESTORED, never what was DEFAULTED". Gated on
// "this blob HAS the field", so an older blob keeps its Drift and Ramp config
// and leaves the new banks at @init's zeros, which is off.
// 2026-09-08: the R22 pitch banks are added, so the magic bumps again and the
// READ accepts all three. A bump rather than a bare append, because appending
// would let an older blob's trailing bytes land in the new banks -- "migrate
// what was RESTORED, never what was DEFAULTED". Gated on "this blob HAS the
// field", so an older blob keeps its drift and ramp config and leaves the pitch
// banks at @init's defaults, which are the 800/600 Hz this plugin always had.
sr_magic = 2300000 + N_TARGETS;
file_var(0, sr_magic);
(sr_magic == 2300000 + N_TARGETS || sr_magic == 2200000 + N_TARGETS || sr_magic == 2100000 + N_TARGETS) ? (
  file_mem(0, speed_ramp_target_value_mem, N_SPEED_TARGETS);
  file_mem(0, speed_ramp_dur_mem,          N_SPEED_TARGETS);
  file_mem(0, speed_ramp_delay_mem,        N_SPEED_TARGETS);
  file_var(0, last_speed_target);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_up,    N_TARGETS);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_down,  N_TARGETS);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_per,   N_TARGETS);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_shape, N_TARGETS);
  file_var(0, last_target_select);
  sr_magic >= 2200000 + N_TARGETS ? (
    file_mem(0, drift_play_mem, N_TARGETS);
    file_mem(0, drift_rest_mem, N_TARGETS);
    file_mem(0, sr_play_mem,    N_SPEED_TARGETS);
    file_mem(0, sr_rest_mem,    N_SPEED_TARGETS);
  );
  sr_magic >= 2300000 + N_TARGETS ? (
    file_mem(0, pitch_note_mem, N_PITCH);
    file_mem(0, pitch_val_mem,  N_PITCH);
    file_mem(0, pitch_mode_mem, N_PITCH);
    file_mem(0, pitch_fine_mem, N_PITCH);
    file_mem(0, pitch_fmod_mem, N_PITCH);
    file_var(0, last_pitch_target);
  );

  // TRACK-DUPLICATE FIX (v2.14). On READ (load/duplicate) file_avail(0) >= 0;
  // on WRITE it is < 0. @serialize is the only section guaranteed to run on
  // both load AND duplicate, so it re-establishes the bank<->slider invariant:
  // force the visible config sliders to match the restored banks for the
  // restored selectors, correcting any transient @slider clobber.
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? (
    slider34 = speed_ramp_target_value_mem[last_speed_target]; // Speed ramp `by`
    slider36 = speed_ramp_dur_mem[last_speed_target];          // Speed ramp duration
    slider40 = speed_ramp_delay_mem[last_speed_target];        // Speed ramp start delay
    slider26 = target_drift_up[last_target_select];            // Drift up
    slider27 = target_drift_down[last_target_select];          // Drift down
    slider28 = target_drift_per[last_target_select];           // Drift period
    slider30 = target_drift_shape[last_target_select];         // Drift shape
    // The four new per-target sliders need this exactly as much as the ones
    // above -- they are backed by live sliders, so they are what a transient
    // @slider can clobber to zero on a track duplicate.
    slider37 = sr_play_mem[last_speed_target];                 // Ramp play for
    slider38 = sr_rest_mem[last_speed_target];                 // Ramp rest for
    slider31 = drift_play_mem[last_target_select];             // Drift play for
    slider32 = drift_rest_mem[last_target_select];             // Drift rest for
    // The pitch block is backed by live sliders too, so it needs the same
    // treatment. `All` reads back from Inhale.
    slider7 = last_pitch_target;
    prs = pitch_read_slot(last_pitch_target);
    slider8  = pitch_note_mem[prs];
    slider9  = pitch_val_mem[prs];
    slider10 = pitch_mode_mem[prs];
    slider11 = pitch_fine_mem[prs];
    slider12 = pitch_fmod_mem[prs];
    // Re-point the mirror at what was just restored, or the next @slider pass
    // reads the restore as five edits and writes them back through All.
    pui_last[0] = slider8;  pui_last[1] = slider9;
    pui_last[2] = slider10; pui_last[3] = slider11;
    pui_last[4] = slider12;
    sliderchange(-1);
  );
);
